{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966798,"nonce":"RUmza5+NiQvTpEI0vC8lJSj7yPQ=","title":"render_tree_with_motion + render_static_layer gated render_paths_overlay_msaa on","message":"On web (`sample_count = 1`):\n- Node-editor SVG icons (tabler outline glyphs via `SvgDocument::render_fit`) invisible until some structural rebuild (double-click on a title) caused a fresh draw pass to \"settle\" the cache differently and incidentally surface them.\n- Subgraph diamond (drawn with `ctx.fill_path(...)` in `blinc_node_editor/src/render.rs`) invisible.\n- Context-menu / popover chrome with curved corners that emit `fill_path` (notch shape, custom shapes) invisible.\n- Zoom-in/out after closing/expanding a node header produced visible artifacts as the half-cached path content flickered.\n\nDesktop (`sample_count \u003e 1`) was unaffected — the MSAA branch dispatched paths normally.\n\n\nEvery path-dispatch site in `crates/blinc_app/src/context.rs` was written as:\n\n```rust\nif use_msaa_overlay \u0026\u0026 batch.has_paths() {\n    self.renderer.render_paths_overlay_msaa(target, batch, self.sample_count);\n}\n```\n\n`use_msaa_overlay = self.sample_count \u003e 1`. When sample_count = 1 (web's webgpu/webgl backend defaults), the entire path-overlay dispatch was skipped. The non-MSAA `render_paths_overlay` already existed in `blinc_gpu` but nothing called it from the app layer.\n\nSeven sites had this shape (in `render_static_layer` and `render_tree_with_motion`):\n- glass-path bg paths\n- glass-path fg paths (unified branch + legacy branch)\n- non-glass-path bg paths\n- non-glass-path fg paths (unified branch — legacy branch had no path dispatch at all)\n- `render_tree_with_motion` glass bg paths\n- `render_tree_with_motion` non-glass z0 paths\n- `render_tree_with_motion` non-glass single-sampled main-pass paths\n\n**Why:** the MSAA branch was the original codepath. The non-MSAA path-dispatch fall-through was never added — the legacy branch in `render_static_layer` was missing path dispatch entirely.\n\n**How to apply:** path dispatch must be MSAA-or-not unconditional. Every `if use_msaa_overlay \u0026\u0026 batch.has_paths()` block should become\n\n```rust\nif batch.has_paths() {\n    if use_msaa_overlay {\n        self.renderer.render_paths_overlay_msaa(target, batch, self.sample_count);\n    } else {\n        self.renderer.render_paths_overlay(target, batch);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWhen adding a new render dispatch site that handles paths, default to this shape. Add the same fallback in any legacy branch that lacks it.\n\n\n- Glyphs route through their own `render_text` / `render_unified` paths and were unaffected — explains why text labels were visible while everything else was missing.\n- `render_rasterized_svgs` handles SVG-as-image primitives, not `SvgDocument::render_fit` which lowers to fill_path. That's why the demo's icons (via `render_fit`) were broken while any rasterized-SVG element would have been fine.","files":null}]}